<title>ITALY: Italy's Breda wins Russian bus contract.</title>
<headline>Italy's Breda wins Russian bus contract.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Breda Costruzioni Ferroviarie, a unit of Finmeccanica, said on Wednesday that it had won a $250 million contract to make buses in Russia.</p>
<p>It said a deal was signed in St Petersburg earlier to set up a company called Severnyjavtobus SpA to co-produce local buses with the participation of Breda, the municipality of St Petersburg and the Severnyjzavod industrial company.</p>
<p>Initial production will be 1,000 buses over four years, rising to 500 buses a year over the following five years.</p>
<p>The deal foresees the participation of Mediocredito Centrale della Cassa di Risparmio di Firenze and Istituto Bancario San Paolo and other international finance groups it did not name. The statement gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 678 2501</p>
